<mxCell id="title" value="B. Oxygen Leak Emergency - Sequence Diagram (Colony.handleEmergency)" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="15" width="1300" height="45" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note" value="Specification: the initial oxygen loss (30) happens once, at detection. If the emergency cannot be handled (no suitable crew + robot pair, or insufficient resources) one additional oxygen loss (30) is applied and the status becomes UNRESOLVED. A repair needs at least 1 available crew member and 1 available robot able to respond to OXYGEN_LEAK, and consumes 2 SPARE_PARTS and 5 BATTERY_POWER. Solid arrows are calls, dashed arrows are returns." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacing=8;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="30" y="65" width="1425" height="74" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
